/* Body binding error test source file, for locals and blocks. Every error in here is deliberate, and
 * was compared with what C# reports for the same code, whose code each description gives, where C# has
 * the construct. The directory parses cleanly, and the point is that each mistake is reported once,
 * where it is, without errors which only follow from others. Run the directory with:
 *
 *     dotnet run --project KeigValCompiler -- <repository root>/tests-body-errors
 *
 * The whole directory gives 177 errors and 0 warnings. Expected from this
 * file, 30 errors:
 *
 *   line 55 ST error 28     a local declared twice in a block (CS0128)
 *   line 56 ST error 29     a local named like a parameter (CS0136)
 *   line 57 ST error 30     a local named like a generic parameter of the function (CS0412)
 *   line 58 ST error 29     a local named like one of a block around (CS0136)
 *   line 59 ST error 29     a local named like one the block around declares after it (CS0136)
 *   line 61 ST error 31     var without a starting value (CS0818)
 *   line 62 ST error 32     var declaring two locals (CS0819)
 *   line 63 ST error 33     var from null (CS0815)
 *   line 64 EX error 62     var from default alone (CS8716)
 *   line 65 ST error 34     a constant declared with var (CS0822)
 *   line 66 ST error 35     a constant of a structure type (CS0283)
 *   line 67 EX error 66     a constant from a field (CS0133)
 *   line 69 EX error 50     var from itself (CS0841)
 *   line 70 EX error 67     a constant from itself (CS0110)
 *   line 74 ST error 29     an inner block's local named like one its block declares after it (CS0136)
 *   line 92 RTMC error 41   a local of a static class (CS0723)
 *   line 93 RTMC error 44   a local of an array of a static class (CS0719)
 *   line 94 GE error 25     a static class as a type argument of a local's type (CS0718)
 *   line 95 RTMC error 41   a var local inferred as a static class (CS0723)
 *   line 96 EX error 75     a constant local of the type object given a string (CS0134)
 *   line 100 EX error 66    a constant local given a variable, and nothing for the constant given it (CS0133)
 *   line 103 ST error 28    a local declared twice in one declaration (CS0128)
 *   line 124 RTMC error 44  an array of a static class in default (CS0719)
 *   line 125 GE error 25    a static class as a type argument in default (CS0718)
 *   line 126 GE error 25    a static class as a type argument before a '.' (CS0718)
 *   line 127 RTMC error 44  an array of a static class as a type argument before a '.' (CS0719)
 *   line 128 GE error 19    a local's type argument not satisfying struct (CS0453)
 *   line 129 GE error 19    a type argument before a '.' not satisfying struct (CS0453)
 *   line 130 GE error 19    a type argument in default not satisfying class (CS0452)
 *   line 131 GE error 19    a type argument's own type argument not satisfying struct (CS0453)
 */

